<PageTitle>Rules | BSAL</PageTitle>

<h1>Rules</h1>

<section>
    <h2>Regular Season</h2>
    <p>
        The regular season consists of weekly best-of-one matchups played across a single division containing all league teams.
        Each week, teams are paired against an opponent — because all teams compete in one division, not every team will face
        every other team over the course of the season.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Format:</strong> Single elimination — a loss ends your run for that matchup.</li>
        <li><strong>Schedule:</strong> One matchup per team per week.</li>
        <li><strong>Division:</strong> All teams compete in a single division; there are no conferences or subdivisions.</li>
        <li><strong>Opponents:</strong> The schedule does not guarantee that every team will play every other team in a given season.</li>
        <li><strong>Season Length:</strong> The number of regular season weeks is variable, ranging from 3 to 6 weeks. The length is determined before each season based on the number of registered teams, with the goal of producing the most competitive and enjoyable experience possible.</li>
    </ul>
</section>
